{"type":"message","id":"349a0ec0","parentId":"f5064b86","timestamp":"2026-03-29T02:57:46.666Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking why I got a 400 status code (no body). Looking at the conversation history, I see that earlier I tried to use sessions_send to send a message to a sub-agent, and it returned a 400 status code error.\n\nLet me review what happened:\n\n1. I tried to send a message to the current session using sessions_send, but got a \"status: 'forbidden'\" error about visibility being restricted to the current session tree.\n\n2. Then I spawned a sub-agent with sessions_spawn and tried to send a message to that sub-agent.\n\n3. That sub-agent task failed with \"⚠️ API rate limit reached.\"\n\nBut the user is specifically asking about a 400 status code (no body). Let me check the actual error messages from the tool calls:\n\n- First sessions_send: returned \"status\": \"forbidden\" - that's a 403 Forbidden, not 400.\n- The sub-agent task failed with \"status\": \"failed\" and message \"⚠️ API rate limit reached.\" - that's not a 400 either.\n\nActually, looking more carefully, the user's question is \"你为何会400 status code (no body)\" - they're asking why there was a 400 status code with no body. This suggests they may have seen a 400 error somewhere, but I don't see a 400 in the recent tool results.\n\nWait, maybe the user is referring to something else? Let me re-read the conversation:\n\n- The user asked: \"lark 机器人可以跨组织添加到群么\" (Can Lark robots be added to groups across organizations?)\n- I responded with \"Lark 机器人可以跨组织添加到群组。\" (Lark robots can be added to groups across organizations.) and explained the conditions.\n- The user then sent a message that appears to be an inter-session message about a subagent task failure due to API rate limit.\n- Then the user asked: \"你为何会400 status code (no body)\"\n\nThis is a bit confusing. Let me look at the transcript more carefully. The inter-session message shows a subagent task completion with status \"failed: ⚠️ API rate limit reached.\" That's not a 400.\n\nMaybe the user is referring to a 400 that occurred elsewhere, or maybe they're referring to the subagent task failure and using \"400 status code\" loosely? Or maybe there's a 400 somewhere I'm not seeing?\n\nI should clarify what the user is referring to. Since I'm not sure exactly what 400 error they're talking about, I should ask for clarification or explain what went wrong based on what I can see.\n\nThe most likely scenario is that the user is referring to the subagent task that failed due to rate limiting, and they're calling it a 400 error (though rate limiting is typically 429, not 400). Or perhaps the API internally returned 400 when we tried to do something.\n\nGiven the context, I think the best approach is to explain what happened with the subagent task and the rate limit issue, and note that if they're seeing a 400 error, it might be related to that or to something else.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"关于400状态码，这可能与API请求的问题相关。根据刚才的操作记录：\n\n1. 我尝试向子代理发送消息时遇到了权限限制（forbidden）\n2. 子代理执行任务时遇到API频率限制（rate limit reached）\n\n400错误通常表示请求存在问题（如参数错误、格式不正确等），而429才是频率限制。如果出现400且没有响应体，可能的原因包括：\n- API端点URL不正确\n- 请求头或参数格式错误\n- 身份验证信息缺失或无效\n\n您是在哪个具体操作中遇到400错误的？可以分享更多上下文，我帮您进一步诊断。"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"openrouter/free","usage":{"input":11073,"output":1533,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":12606,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774753054161,"responseId":"gen-1774753054-dNRNoFWiCEM59hsjmmf5"}}
